Blueberry__4_sec2.text:
•   The pathogens survive from year to year in infected stems; spores are spread by wind or rain;
       Phomopsis infects stems through flowers (LSU).
   •   Incidence increases when plants have been stressed by cold or drought injury (UCT).

Pepper,_bell__3_glance.text:
Yellow patches on the upper leaf surface and white powdery growth underneath, leading to leaf
shedding. A serious and growing problem for chilli in India. Sprays at first appearance are the main control;
CIB&RC lists the largest number of products of any chilli disease for this one.

Potato__10_sec2.text:
•   Pathogen: Synchytrium endobioticum, a soil-borne biotrophic fungus that causes potato wart (SPR).
   •   Quarantine: wart is a notifiable disease in India, restricted to the Darjeeling hills of West Bengal (AGR;
       supplementary source).

Tomato__10_glance.text:
Small water-soaked leaf spots with a yellow halo, scabby fruit spots and defoliation of older
leaves, spread by rain splash. TNAU's recommendation is disease-free seed plus streptocycline sprays;
CIB&RC lists a tomato bacterial leaf spot claim.
